s/kbolton-lab/ArCH/issues/9/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/kbolton-lab/ArCH/issues/9/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/kbolton-lab/ArCH/issues/9", "id": 2393796934, "node_id": "I_kwDOG-Zs786OrnFG", "number": 9, "title": "Compatibility of ArCH with UK Biobank WGS/WES CRAM data", "user": {"login": "XUEbaogai0101", "id": 103372530, "node_id": "U_kgDOBilW8g", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103372530?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101", "html_url": "https://github.com/XUEbaogai0101", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2024-07-07T00:23:52Z", "updated_at": "2024-07-11T02:36:12Z", "closed_at": "2024-07-11T02:36:12Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Dear developers,\r\n\r\nArCH has been incredibly useful and well-designed for analyzing sequencing data. Thank you for your hard work and dedication to this project!\r\n\r\nI'm interested in using ArCH for analyzing UK Biobank (UKB) whole-genome sequencing (WGS) or whole-exome sequencing (WES) data.     These data are stored in CRAM format. I have a few questions regarding the compatibility and potential use of ArCH with this dataset:\r\n\r\n1. The UKB sequencing data might not include UMI information. How critical is this for ArCH's performance, and are there any workarounds?\r\n\r\n2. The sequencing depth of UKB WGS/WES data may differ from the targeted deep sequencing used in ArCH's validation. How might this affect the detection of low-frequency variants, particularly those below 0.5% VAF?\r\n\r\n3. ArCH was initially optimized for a specific panel of clonal hematopoiesis genes. Are there any considerations or modifications needed when applying it to WGS/WES data covering a broader genomic region?\r\n\r\n4.  Are there any other potential challenges or adjustments we should be aware of when using ArCH with UKB WGS/WES data?\r\n\r\nThank you for your time and assistance. Any insights or suggestions would be greatly appreciated.\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nXue", "closed_by": {"login": "XUEbaogai0101", "id": 103372530, "node_id": "U_kgDOBilW8g", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103372530?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101", "html_url": "https://github.com/XUEbaogai0101", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/XUEbaogai0101/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/user